<title>GERMANY: Unilever pulls gene-soy from German market.</title>
<headline>Unilever pulls gene-soy from German market.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Dutch group Unilever's German subsidiary said on Thursday it would stop selling food products containing edible oils derived from genetically modified soy beans.</p>
<p>A company spokesman said consumer resistance to gene-soy products meant they could not be sold in Germany.</p>
<p>Environmentalist groups Greenpeace had also called for a boycott of gene-soy, citing health fears. First imports came onto the German market from the U.S. earlier in the autumn.</p>
<p>The spokesman added U.S. farmers would should consider separating their gene-modified and normal soy crops next year if they were to expect to gain access to the European market.</p>
<p>--Bonn newsroom +49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
